# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# rm: ~/.config/TikuEditorPreferences
# A line of a program, coloured by what its parts MEAN -- end to end,
# through the application the person actually types into.
#
# The two pixels below were probed rather than guessed, and they are
# GLYPH pixels: the ink a letter is drawn with, not chrome.  Each is
# asserted twice, before and after, so what is proven is the CHANGE --
# this stretch of the line stopped being ordinary ink and became the
# shade the theme names for what it means.
wait 14
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Documents
wait 4
menu-pick Editor
wait 90
expect-title Edit
note one line of TikuOS BASIC, typed into the editor a key at a time
key 1
wait 3
key 0
wait 3
key space
wait 3
key P
wait 3
key R
wait 3
key I
wait 3
key N
wait 3
key T
wait 3
key space
wait 3
key A
wait 12
shot /tmp/tiku-editor-plain.png
note an unnamed document is plain text: every byte is the document's ink
expect-pixel 267 145 080808
expect-pixel 299 145 000000
note the Language menu, right of Text on the bar, names the language
click 314 8
wait 6
expect-menu BASIC
menu-pick BASIC
wait 20
shot /tmp/tiku-editor-syntax.png
note as BASIC the line number is faint: ordinary ink halfway to the page
expect-pixel 267 145 838383
note and PRINT takes the theme's ink for a reserved word
expect-pixel 299 145 0000b0
note Plain Text from the same menu puts both back to the document's ink
click 314 8
wait 6
expect-menu Plain Text
menu-pick Plain Text
wait 20
expect-pixel 267 145 080808
expect-pixel 299 145 000000
note and the editor is put away rather than left standing: a script
note that leaks a running application poisons the one after it.  Its
note tab first: the bar took the keyboard when its menu was opened, and
note a key aimed at an application has to be aimed at its window.
click-window Edit
wait 6
key Escape
wait 8
expect-title Edit
note Escape in the question presses Cancel, the safe road: still standing
key Escape
wait 6
expect-title Edit
note asked again, Return cancels; an explicit Discard click closes it
key Escape
wait 6
key Return
wait 8
expect-title Edit
key Escape
wait 6
click 592 318
wait 60
expect-no-title Edit
quit
